{"lines":[{"t":"G","y":0.66424418581207578,"x":0.065843621286484841,"w":0.022633744875590001,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"t":"Reading","x":0.82820131113180195,"y":0.061334893669920842,"h":0.019229136310842443,"c":1,"w":0.084386157989501998},{"w":0.74279836018880208,"y":0.10895170801951859,"t":"to categorizing them by shape (circle or triangle), they do so more quickly than","h":0.017501780506578912,"c":1,"x":0.11728394736183437},{"c":1,"t":"monolingual people, reflecting better cognitive control when having to make rapid","w":0.76543207804361979,"y":0.12632508814903276,"x":0.11934157387198961,"h":0.017667844522968212},{"w":0.19341564178466797,"x":0.1193415617026793,"c":1,"h":0.017470964694612845,"y":0.14389534866764608,"t":"changes of strategy."},{"t":"It also seems that the neurological roots of the bilingual advantage extend to brain","h":0.020298723056824675,"x":0.1068944201080733,"w":0.78621520996093741,"c":1,"y":0.16983403587529522},{"t":"aireas more traditionally associated with sensory processing. When monolingual","w":0.75514404296875004,"h":0.016012340046912987,"x":0.1193415586701633,"c":1,"y":0.19040697659769434},{"y":0.20640885100913464,"t":"aind bilingual adolescents listen to simple speech sounds without any intervening","x":0.11928526737969075,"w":0.75938446044921881,"c":1,"h":0.018904262493299684},{"c":1,"w":0.68312759399414069,"y":0.22526501737579063,"h":0.018921028739291135,"x":0.11934155264463887,"t":"background noise, they show highly similar brain stem responses. When"},{"x":0.11719784131836121,"t":"researchers play the same sound to both groups in the presence of background","w":0.75326939900716139,"h":0.020089829066336051,"c":1,"y":0.24140859327654218},{"t":"noise, however, the bilingual listeners' neural response is considerably larger,","x":0.11934156226265107,"y":0.26017441880754344,"w":0.73045267740885422,"h":0.018977524675385049,"c":1},{"w":0.78410263061523433,"c":1,"h":0.019469583554037495,"t":"reflecting better encoding of the sound's fundamental frequency, a feature of sound","x":0.11721058137141398,"y":0.27759290724205266},{"x":0.11728395143324438,"y":0.29651162774951678,"t":"closely related to pitch perception.","h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"w":0.32716049194335944},{"x":0.11728394924967234,"h":0.017450420819968948,"t":"Such improvements in cognitive and sensory processing may help a bilingual","y":0.3241279068173224,"w":0.73045267740885411,"c":1},{"y":0.34100205989459087,"t":"person to process information in the environment, and help explain why bilingual","x":0.11723893430417548,"h":0.018236602855093764,"w":0.76345957438151046,"c":1},{"y":0.3604240283831659,"h":0.016029460129664885,"t":"aclults acquire a third language better than monolingual adults master a second","x":0.11728394640333165,"w":0.74897120157877617,"c":1},{"w":0.75102879842122394,"h":0.017667844522968101,"x":0.11522634141486435,"y":0.37779740850446064,"t":"la nguage. This advantage may be rooted in the skill of focussing on information","c":1},{"c":1,"w":0.72447143554687499,"h":0.019099964550723825,"t":"about the new language while reducing interference from the languages they","x":0.11720073279237539,"y":0.39407968615811517},{"t":"al ready know.","x":0.11725771467149704,"w":0.13379732767740887,"h":0.017643771828695254,"c":1,"y":0.41268974166036976},{"t":"Research also indicates that bilingual experience may help to keep the cognitive","w":0.7573553466796874,"h":0.019164385306961407,"y":0.43997637001689816,"c":1,"x":0.11720458106092053},{"x":0.11522634675887938,"w":0.77160491943359366,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1,"t":"mechanisms sharp by recruiting alternate brain networks to compensate for those","y":0.45930232543521243},{"c":1,"t":"that become damaged during aging. Older bilinguals enjoy improved memory","w":0.73045267740885411,"h":0.017448708362377219,"y":0.47673733830280618,"x":0.11522633606014883},{"w":0.75514404296875015,"x":0.1131687191471147,"y":0.49411071843739784,"h":0.0175171886933847,"t":"relative to monolingual people, which can lead to real-world health benefits. In a","c":1},{"y":0.51002967743568961,"x":0.11512232614579546,"w":0.77802185058593754,"h":0.021988429506479279,"c":1,"t":"study of over 200 patients with Alzheimer's disease, a degenerative brain disease,"},{"y":0.52928826043075872,"x":0.11516362144876088,"h":0.018730330944622953,"c":1,"w":0.73880737304687505,"t":"bilingual patients reported showing initial symptoms of the disease an average"},{"c":1,"x":0.11508915756672858,"y":0.54542320692451551,"w":0.73073145548502605,"h":0.022111209739082982,"t":"of five years later than monolingual patients. In a follow-up study, researchers"},{"x":0.11513370982769128,"y":0.56374604192743805,"h":0.020614327474533511,"t":"compared the brains of bilingual and monolingual patients matched on the severity","w":0.78004531860351567,"c":1},{"y":0.58274440520458304,"t":"of Alzheimer's symptoms. Surprisingly, the bilinguals'brains had more physical","w":0.74485595703124996,"h":0.019140164899882239,"c":1,"x":0.11522634232262874},{"t":"signs of disease than their monolingual counterparts, even though their outward","c":1,"h":0.017513764901492479,"x":0.11522634957780838,"y":0.60174418588703937,"w":0.75308639526367183},{"c":1,"x":0.11503701114744597,"y":0.61573634551945777,"t":"behaviour and abilities were the same. If the brain is an engine, bilingualism may","w":0.76374308268229174,"h":0.023592424336535633},{"x":0.11316872260569161,"t":"help it to go farther on the same amount of fuel.","y":0.63808139520145934,"w":0.45473251342773441,"h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1},{"t":"Furthermore, the benefits associated with bilingual experience seem to start","x":0.10288064878106619,"y":0.66424418588392031,"h":0.017441860778592999,"c":1,"w":0.72839508056640623},{"h":0.018979475832378578,"x":0.11311261912762281,"t":"very early. In one study, researchers taught seven-month-old babies growing","y":0.68163291167470796,"w":0.72439844767252604,"c":1},{"w":0.74095392862955733,"c":1,"h":0.020680409578608727,"t":"up in monolingual or bilingual homes that when they heard a tinkling sound, a","x":0.10482576787170843,"y":0.69891274795953018},{"x":0.11316872638317031,"w":0.7633744812011718,"y":0.71937573600110571,"t":"puppet appeared on one side of a screen. Haltway through the study, the puppet","c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185},{"x":0.11308592475260222,"c":1,"y":0.73506109079777748,"t":"began appearing on the opposite side of the screen. In order to get a reward, the","w":0.76353190104166657,"h":0.019643064662901888},{"c":1,"y":0.75236592114067558,"x":0.11101699031663316,"t":"infants had to adjust the rule they'd learned; only the bilingual babies were able to","w":0.77384831746419269,"h":0.0203021648213777},{"y":0.77179034158619797,"w":0.77572016398111976,"t":"successfully learn the new rule. This suggests that for very young children, as well","x":0.11316872440947436,"h":0.017453844611860947,"c":1},{"y":0.78916020618686866,"t":"as for older people, navigating a multilingual environment imparts advantages that","h":0.018756639550234877,"x":0.11311667296937515,"w":0.77787724812825521,"c":1},{"x":0.11111110578598214,"y":0.80800942277261378,"t":"transfer far beyond language.","w":0.28395062764485673,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"x":0.87448559623210254,"y":0.93604651143122397,"t":"47","w":0.026748971939086985,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1},{"y":0.96768258536995222,"t":"leltsresources.org","x":0.39483721299237268,"h":0.016454192297478354,"w":0.20824633280436194,"c":1}],"w":2400,"h":3395}